QT-WR02 log: late first-install failure notice and the mover's earlier-result alert; 1.8.1 rig build of 65925382 (executable sha256 778bd91d75024767...), DMG sha256 79c13a8e7ce211a2...
--- notes
VM portty-test (macOS 27.2), user admin. Prior state: the RC-WR02 end state (post-fix 1.8.1 rig build of
83df1e1f, executable sha256 f6a9cb6c8b92f3e5..., GUI and daemon running, no sessions). It was copied to
~/qtwr02-bak (app and config files), removed by r9.sh prep none, and restored afterwards (same sha256,
GUI and daemon started, no sessions, update.log/update_notified/settings.json/daemon.log* put back,
Downloads consent reset, ~/p18 and the backup removed).
Method: RC-WR02's (p18rc/vm/wr02.sh run): the DMG copied into ~/Downloads as the release asset name,
unquarantined, opened, then `open /Volumes/Portty/Portty.app` (T0). A watcher flips ~/p18/verify-mode
from adhoc to off the moment the installer process exists, so only the installer's re-verify runs the
real codesign on the ad-hoc copy and fails. Notification evidence: `log show` of usernoted and
NotificationCenter over the row window, then Notification Center opened (click on the menu-bar clock)
and read with axdump. Step 2: the DMG re-opened from ~/Downloads and its app opened again, with
verify-mode back to adhoc; the alert read with axdump and a screenshot before OK.
Focus caveat: the VM has a Focus (Do Not Disturb) on from before this row (moon in the menu bar, an
activity-manager assertion in ~/Library/DoNotDisturb/DB/Assertions.json). usernoted presented the
notice as a banner, and NotificationCenter then muted the on-screen banner ("muted by DND suppression:
delay") and added it to the history. So no banner was drawn on screen in this run; the notice was
delivered and is in Notification Center. The Focus was left as it was.
Clock: timed's last NTP receipt before and during the row was in step (16:40:55, received == log
time); no "Received time" or adjustment between 16:40:55 and 16:47:18. No step inside the row.
The step-1 0.4 s poller timeline was overwritten by step 2's poller (same file); step 1 is covered by
run.txt, check.txt, update.log, the usernoted lines and the screenshots.
